<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds await summit news, some short activity.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds await summit news, some short activity.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1100 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> June 1999 7.50 pct   107.25/35 (+0.01)   bid yield 3.65 (UNCHD)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		115.02/12 (+0.06)		 4.58 (-0.02)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct   101.48/56 (+0.09)		 5.54 (-0.02)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		114.85/05 (+0.13)		 6.31 (-0.01)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (Sept)	  101.78 (+0.21)</p>
<p> TREASURIES (June)   112.22 (-0.06 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1247 (PREV 1.1248)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 +0.05	LEVEL	  10-2 yr  189     (189)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.13	-0.15	  10-5 yr   94	(96)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.15	-0.17</p>
<p>--------------------------(June 16)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds barely changed from opening, sidelined as developments on EMU awaited from EU summit in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>* But cash activity focusses on short end with buyers chasing 1998/99 paper mainly, selling German paper.</p>
<p>* Spread to Germany narrows as guilder paper underperforms.</p>
<p>-- Garry West, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
